    ticketHelp: {
      rowTitle: 'Tickets and printer',
      rowSub: 'How to print, reprint, edit or create a ticket',
      intro: 'Every order has a receipt-style ticket: customer, type (delivery, takeaway, dine-in), items with quantities and prices, customer note, total, pickup or delivery code. It prints on your thermal printer or through your device\'s print dialog.',
      howTitle: 'Printing a ticket, step by step',
      how1: 'Open the Fairide app (installed on your tablet, phone or PC), turn on your Bluetooth thermal printer and go to Orders.',
      how2: 'In the “Ticket printer” card, tap “Connect my printer” and pick it in the list. To be redone when you reopen the app: the system requires it, not Fairide.',
      how3: 'Print a test ticket: if it comes out, everything is ready. Choose the paper (58 or 80 mm) according to your printer.',
      how4: 'Then the 🖨️ button on each order prints its ticket in one click; the order detail also offers “Print the ticket”, “×2” and “Print the delivery note”.',
      autoTitle: 'Automatic printing',
      auto1: 'Tick “Print every new order automatically” in the Printer card: every paid order comes out as soon as it arrives, hands-free.',
      auto2: 'Keep the Orders tab open and the printer connected during service. An order is never auto-printed twice.',
      editTitle: 'Reprint, edit, create a ticket',
      edit1: 'First print failed (paper jam, printer off)? Open the order and click “Print again” as many times as needed; the detail shows how many times the ticket already came out. Nothing changes for the order.',
      edit2: '“Edit the ticket” opens the editor: fix a label, remove or add a line, add a note (allergy, no onions…), choose the number of copies, then print. The saved order stays intact, only the paper changes.',
      edit3: '“New manual ticket” (Printer card) creates a ticket from scratch: phone order, dine-in table, kitchen slip. It prints via Bluetooth or the print dialog; it is not saved as an order.',
      deviceTitle: 'Which device, which printer',
      device1: 'Direct Bluetooth from the app: Android tablet or phone, Windows PC, Mac or Chromebook (app installed from Chrome or Edge). ESC/POS thermal printer with Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE), 58 or 80 mm paper (Xprinter, Munbyn, Goojprt, Netum, Phomemo, “BLE” models).',
      device2: 'iPad and iPhone: the web app has no Bluetooth access (Apple limitation). From 1 October 2026 the Fairide app from the App Store will print over Bluetooth directly. Until then: “Print the delivery note” with an AirPrint or Wi-Fi printer, or an Android tablet at the counter for the thermal printer.',
      device3: 'USB, Wi-Fi or network printer (Epson, Star…): install it on the device like any printer, then “Print the delivery note”. On Android, the free RawBT app also sends the ticket to a thermal printer.',
      troubleTitle: 'Nothing comes out?',
      trouble1: 'The printer does not appear in the list: check it is on, BLE (not classic Bluetooth), and not already paired to another device.',
      trouble2: '“No printer connected” after a reload: that is normal, reconnect it in one click.',
      trouble3: 'Truncated ticket or odd characters: switch to 58 mm if the printer is small, and check the roll.',
      trouble4: 'Still nothing: “Print the delivery note” goes through the device\'s print dialog and works with any installed printer. And write to us from Support.',
      contentTitle: 'What the ticket contains',
      contentText: 'Business name and address, order number and time, type, customer and phone, items with quantities and prices, customer note and instructions, subtotal, delivery, discount, total, pickup or delivery code. Accents are simplified on the thermal ticket (“Creme brulee”) to stay readable on every model.',
      goOrders: 'Open the Orders page →'
    },
